# LiDAR Processing Scripts

A collection of R scripts for processing LiDAR data using the lidR package for forest analysis applications.

## Overview

This repository contains scripts for processing airborne LiDAR point cloud data to extract forest structure metrics, generate canopy models, and perform tree detection analysis.

## Scripts

### Data Processing
- [ ] **01_data_preprocessing.R** - Point cloud filtering and ground classification
- [ ] **02_normalization.R** - Height normalization above ground
- [ ] **03_chm_generation.R** - Canopy Height Model creation

### Metrics Extraction  
- [ ] **04_grid_metrics.R** - Forest structure metrics at grid resolution
- [ ] **05_zonal_statistics.R** - Summary statistics by management units
- [ ] **06_custom_metrics.R** - User-defined metric calculations

### Tree Analysis
- [ ] **07_tree_detection.R** - Individual tree detection and segmentation
- [ ] **08_crown_delineation.R** - Tree crown polygon generation
- [ ] **09_tree_metrics.R** - Individual tree measurements

### Utilities
- [ ] **utils/processing_functions.R** - Custom processing functions
- [ ] **utils/validation_tools.R** - Quality control and validation
- [ ] **config/parameters.R** - Processing parameters and settings

## Requirements

```r
# Required R packages
library(lidR)
library(terra)
library(sf)
library(future)
library(parallel)
```

## Input Data

- LAS/LAZ files (normalized or raw point clouds)
- Management unit boundaries (optional)
- Digital Elevation Model (optional)

## Output Products

- Canopy Height Models (GeoTIFF)
- Forest metrics grids
- Tree location points
- Crown boundary polygons
- Summary statistics tables

